## Introduction to LLMs

### What are Large Language Models?
Large Language Models (LLMs) are advanced AI systems trained on massive text datasets to:
- Understand natural language
- Generate human-like text
- Perform complex language tasks
- Adapt to various domains

![LLM Evolution Timeline](https://example.com/llm-evolution.png)

### Key Characteristics:
| Feature | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| Scale | Billions of parameters |
| Training Data | Terabytes of text |
| Architecture | Transformer-based |
| Capabilities | Text generation, translation, Q&A |

---

## LLM Architecture Deep Dive

### Transformer Architecture
The foundation of modern LLMs:

![Transformer Diagram](https://example.com/transformer-arch.png)

#### Core Components:
1. **Encoder Stack** (Understanding)
   - Processes input text
   - Creates contextual representations

2. **Decoder Stack** (Generation)
   - Produces output text
   - Uses attention mechanisms

### Attention Mechanisms
The "secret sauce" of LLMs:

```python
# Simplified self-attention formula
attention = softmax((Q @ K.T) / sqrt(d_k)) @ V
Types of Attention:

Self-attention (within same sequence)

Cross-attention (between sequences)

Multi-head attention (parallel attention layers)

